-- Passage wg9-narrative-writing-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('103a1107-a284-5605-bfbd-80966fd173e4', 'wg9-narrative-writing-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Lake Ice$q$, $q$(1) For three weeks, I had been working on a blue bowl for the spring art show at Westfield High. (2) It was the first piece I had ever shaped on the pottery wheel without Mr. Adeyemi's hands steadying mine, and its walls were thin and even. (3) On Thursday, I dipped it in a glaze called Lake Ice and set it on the kiln shelf with everyone else's work.

(4) On Friday morning, the whole class crowded around the kiln as Mr. Adeyemi lifted the lid. (5) Warm air rolled out and fogged my glasses. (6) One by one, he passed out mugs, tiles, and small vases. (7) Then he held up my bowl, and the room went quiet. (8) A crack ran from the rim almost to the base, thin as a hair.

(9) "It happens," he said. (10) "Clay remembers everything, even an air bubble you never saw." (11) I wanted to drop the bowl in the trash and walk out of the room. (12) Instead, I turned it slowly in my hands and noticed how the glaze had pooled inside the crack, turning it a deeper blue than the rest of the bowl. (13) The art room also has a supply closet full of paint, yarn, and old magazines.

(14) That weekend, I wrote a small card to sit beside the bowl at the show. (15) It said, "Lake Ice, with one fault line." (16) The show was on Tuesday.$q$, 'draft')
