-- Passage wg9-narrative-writing-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f664fd65-416f-5b05-b55d-097ce2c98b9d', 'wg9-narrative-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Sale in the Community Room$q$, $q$(1) Every June, the Friends of the Ashby Library hold a book sale on the front lawn, and this year I was in charge of the children's tables. (2) I had spent two Saturdays sorting picture books, chapter books, and comics into labeled boxes. (3) At eight in the morning, the sky was clear. (4) By eight thirty, it was not.

(5) The first raindrops tapped on the canvas awnings, and then the storm arrived all at once. (6) Volunteers grabbed boxes and ran for the doors. (7) Mr. Osei, who organized the sale, stood on the library steps holding a soggy sign. (8) "We can't sell wet books," he said. (9) I looked through the window at the library's community room, which was empty except for stacked chairs.

(10) "What if we move everything inside?" I asked. (11) He hesitated, then nodded. (12) For the next hour, a line of volunteers passed boxes hand to hand from the lawn to the community room. (13) The library was built in 1923 with money raised by local families. (14) We pushed tables against the walls and taped the labels back on.

(15) At ten o'clock, we opened the doors. (16) Families shook off their umbrellas and came in, and the room filled with the sound of children reading titles aloud to each other. (17) We sold more books than the year before.$q$, 'draft')
