   $q$How does sentence 4 prepare readers for later events in the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It hints that indoor practice may not be enough, which sets up the narrator getting lost in real terrain.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the narrator is an expert runner who will win the meet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It introduces the conflict between the narrator and a rival runner.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"invents-conflict"},{"text":"It explains that the meet was moved indoors because of bad weather.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It hints that indoor practice may not be enough, which sets up the narrator getting lost in real terrain.$q$, $q$By noting that the gym had no hills, sentence 4 suggests the narrator is not fully ready for the forest, which foreshadows the trouble at control six. The meet clearly takes place outdoors in a state forest.$q$, 'draft', '3038fc80-0533-5a65-8633-c82595a9f2f4')
